// Package security restricts what a container's processes may do, on top
// of the isolation that namespaces give.
//
// Three modes (see Mode):
//   - none: namespaces only.
//   - baseline (Phase 4, default): Docker's default capability set and
//     seccomp profile, masked and read-only /proc and /sys paths, and
//     no_new_privs.
//   - policy (Phase 5): enforces a PolicyFile generated by `minibox
//     profile`. Only the observed syscalls are allowed (everything else gets
//     EPERM), only the inferred capabilities are kept, and the root
//     filesystem is read-only except the observed writable paths.
//
// The seccomp filter is compiled to BPF by this package (seccomp.go) from
// either Docker's own JSON profile (docker.go) or the policy's allowlist.
package security
